- @lpolice_loyalty: Bolster the loyalty of the police.
- @lpolice_strength: Recruit additional police.
- @lbureaucracy: Purge the bureaucracy of <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> elements.
- @lban_sa: Ban the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span>, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazi</span> paramilitary group.
- @lban_sh: Ban the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span>, the Nationalist paramilitary.
- @lunban_rfb: Reverse the <span style="color: #8B0000;">**RFB**</span> ban.
- @lfree_kpd: Protect <span style="color: #8B0000;">**KPD**</span> demonstrations from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>.


@lpolice_loyalty
view-if: prussian_police_loyalty < 1
on-arrival: prussian_police_loyalty += 0.15; rfb_strength += 25; reichsexekution += 1; prussia_action_timer += 7

The police have historically been overrun with <span style="color: #808080;">reactionaries</span>, and we are trying to change this, little by little. We have improved the training and recruitment process to select for a broader demographic than the traditional <span style="color: #3E88B3;">conservatives</span>, and to put a tighter leash on their political activity. In addition, we set up committees to investigate the ranks of the police and remove those with <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> sympathies. The <span style="color: [+ kpd_colour +];">**KPD**</span> have also began to infiltrate some of their own into the police force...

Current police loyalty: [+ prussian_police_loyalty : loyalty +].

@lpolice_strength
on-arrival: prussian_police_strength += 30; rfb_strength += 50; prussia_action_timer += 9

We have increased the size of the Prussian police.

@lbureaucracy
on-arrival: prussia_purge += 1; prussian_police_loyalty += 0.08; nationalism -= 5; pacifism += 1; democratization += 2; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 4; coup_progress += 0.5; dvp_left += 2; ddp_left += 1; lvp_left += 1.5; reichsexekution += 1; bureaucracy_goal_prussia -= 1; new_middle_kpd += 2; prussia_action_timer += 6; prussia_jud += 0.8

The bureaucracy is deeply <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span>, and many abuse their power to favor the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">political right</span>. By removing the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">pro-monarchy</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">pro-dictatorship</span> elements, we can democratize it. The <span style="color: [+ kpd_colour +];">**KPD**</span> have also began to infiltrate some of their own into the state bureaucracy...

@lban_sa
view-if: sa_banned == 0
on-arrival: sa_strength *= 0.9; sa_strength *= 0.75 if prussian_police_loyalty >= 0.75; sa_banned_pro = 1 if prussian_police_loyalty >= 0.75; sa_banned_pro = 0 if prussian_police_loyalty < 0.75; sa_banned = 1; dvp_relation -= 3; prussian_police_loyalty -= 0.05; sa_militancy -= 0.05; sa_ban_timer = 6; interior_goal_prussia -= 1; coup_progress -= 2 if coup_progress >= 6; prussia_action_timer += 5

As it turns out, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazi</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> has many allies in the police and bureaucracy. Our relationship with the police weakens, and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> can still organize illegally, right under the police's noses. [? if sa_banned_pro : Nevertheless, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> is substantially weakened by our ban. ?] 

[? if coup_progress >= 6: There are reports of an imminent coup by the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>. We have disrupted some of these plans, but the threat is still present. ?]

@lban_sh
on-arrival: sh_strength *= 0.85; sh_strength *= 0.7 if prussian_police_loyalty >= 0.75; sh_banned = 1; dvp_relation -= 5; lvp_relation -= 2; prussian_police_loyalty -= 0.1; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government = 1 and in_grand_coalition = 1 and president = "Hindenburg"; sh_ban_timer = 6; interior_goal_prussia -= 1; sh_coup_progress = coup_progress; coup_progress -= 1 if coup_progress >= 6; hindenburg_angry += 5; prussia_action_timer += 6
view-if: sh_banned == 0

[? if president == "Hindenburg": Banning the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span> weakens our relationship with President Hindenburg, as well as the political <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> and the police. ?][? if president != "Hindenburg": Banning the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span> weakens our relationship with the political <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> and the police. ?] [? if spd_in_government = 1 and in_grand_coalition = 1 and president = "Hindenburg" : It also weakens our coalition due to the influence of Hindenburg on the <span style="color: #C0A054;">right</span> wing of our coalition. ?] In addition, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span> still operates out of public sight. 

@lunban_rfb
view-if: rfb_banned = 1
on-arrival: rfb_banned = 0; rfb_strength += 100; prussian_police_loyalty -= 0.1; rfb_goal_prussia -= 1; hindenburg_angry += 8; prussia_action_timer += 3; prussia_jud -= 0.3

The <span style="color: #700000;">Communist</span> <span style="color: #700000;">**RFB**</span> is no longer banned.

@lfree_kpd
view-if: rfb_banned = 0
on-arrival: rfb_banned = 0; rfb_strength += 50; rfb_militancy += 0.03; prussian_police_loyalty -= 0.05; workers_kpd += 4; unemployed_kpd += 4; free_kpd_goal_prussia -= 1; reichsexekution += 1; dvp_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 5; z_relation -= 4; dvp_right += 2; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 0.5; lvp_right += 1.5; left_dissent -= 5; reformist_dissent += 5; prussia_action_timer += 8

Restrictions are lifted and police are deployed to protect <span style="color: #700000;">Communist</span> demonstrations and organizations from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>.


@spd_policies_prussia
choose-if: prussia_spd == 1 and prussia_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not prussia_spd == 1: We are not part of the Coalition. ?][? if prussia_spd == 1 and prussia_action_timer > 0: We have to wait [+ prussia_action_timer +] months before our next action. ?]
view-if: prussia_gov == "SPD"


- @spolice_loyalty: Bolster the loyalty of the police.
- @spolice_strength: Recruit additional police.
- @sbureaucracy: Purge the bureaucracy of <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> elements.
- @sban_sa: Ban the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span>, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazi</span> paramilitary group.
- @sprosecute_sa: Target the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span>, and minimize their disruptions.
- @sunban_sa: Reverse the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> ban.
- @sban_ph: Ban the <span style="color: #8B0000;">Proletarische Hundertschaften</span>.
- @sunban_ph: Reverse the <span style="color: #8B0000;">Proletarische Hundertschaften</span> ban.
- @sban_rfb: Ban the <span style="color: #8B0000;">**RFB**</span>, the <span style="color: #700000;">Communist</span> paramilitary.
- @sunban_rfb: Reverse the <span style="color: #8B0000;">**RFB**</span> ban.
- @sban_sh: Ban the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span>, the Nationalist paramilitary.
- @sunban_sh: Reverse the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span> ban.
- @snegotiate_concordat: Negotiate a concordat with the Vatican.
- @ssign_concordat: Sign a concordat with the Vatican.


@spolice_loyalty
view-if: prussian_police_loyalty < 1
on-arrival: prussian_police_loyalty += 0.15; prussia_action_timer += 5

The police have historically been overrun with <span style="color: #808080;">reactionaries</span>, and we are trying to change this, little by little. We have improved the training and recruitment process to select for a broader demographic than the traditional <span style="color: #3E88B3;">conservatives</span>, and to put a tighter leash on their political activity. In addition, we set up committees to investigate the ranks of the police and remove those with <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> sympathies. It is a slow and arduous work.

Current police loyalty: [+ prussian_police_loyalty : loyalty +].

@spolice_strength
on-arrival: prussian_police_strength += 35; prussia_action_timer += 6

We have increased the size of the Prussian police.

@sbureaucracy
on-arrival: prussia_purge += 1; prussian_police_loyalty += 0.08; nationalism -= 4; pacifism += 1; democratization += 1; pro_republic += 4*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; prussia_action_timer += 6; prussia_jud += 1.5

The bureaucracy is deeply <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span>, and many abuse their power to favor the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">political right</span>. By removing the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">pro-monarchy</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">pro-dictatorship</span> elements, we can democratize it. Some of our opponents claim that we are infringing on individual freedoms, but perhaps the security of the republic requires it.

@sban_sa
view-if: nazi_urgency >= 3 and sa_banned == 0
choose-if: not sa_ban_repealed and (prussia_coup_win or not otl_prussian_coup_seen)
unavailable-subtitle: [+ chancellor +] has threatened a <i>Reichsexekution</i>, if we don't follow the orders of his decree.
on-arrival: sa_strength *= 0.85; sa_strength *= 0.75 if prussian_police_loyalty >= 0.75; sa_banned_pro = 1 if prussian_police_loyalty >= 0.75; sa_banned_pro = 0 if prussian_police_loyalty < 0.75; sa_banned = 1; dvp_relation -= 3; prussian_police_loyalty -= 0.05; sa_militancy -= 0.05; sa_ban_timer = 6; coup_progress -= 2 if coup_progress >= 6; prussia_action_timer += 5

As it turns out, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazi</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> has many allies in the police and bureaucracy. Our relationship with the police weakens, and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> can still organize illegally, right under the police's noses. [? if sa_banned_pro : Nevertheless, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> is substantially weakened by our ban. ?] 

[? if coup_progress >= 6: There are reports of an imminent coup by the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>. We have disrupted some of these plans, but the threat is still present. ?]

@sprosecute_sa
view-if: nazi_urgency >= 3 and not sa_banned and (chancellor == "Papen" or chancellor == "Schleicher")
on-arrival: sa_strength *= 0.95; sa_militancy -= 0.02; prussian_police_loyalty -= 0.02; sa_strength *= 0.98 if prussian_police_loyalty >= 0.75; prussia_action_timer += 6

While an outright ban on the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> may be out of reach, we can make life as difficult as possible for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Storm Troopers</span>. The most reckless among them can be prosecuted on charges of murder and related crimes, and we can ensure legal public demonstrations and meetings are protected from their unlawful disruptions.

@sunban_sa
view-if: sa_banned = 1
on-arrival: sa_banned = 0; sa_strength += 100; sa_militancy += 0.05; coup_progress += 2 if sa_coup_progress >= 6; prussia_action_timer += 8

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> is no longer banned. They immediately go on a recruiting spree.

@sban_sh
on-arrival: sh_strength *= 0.8; sh_strength *= 0.7 if prussian_police_loyalty >= 0.75; sh_banned = 1; dvp_relation -= 5; lvp_relation -= 2; prussian_police_loyalty -= 0.1; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government = 1 and in_grand_coalition = 1 and president = "Hindenburg"; coalition_dissent += 1 if prussia_gov == "Social-Catholic" and cvp_formed; sh_ban_timer = 6; sh_coup_progress = coup_progress; coup_progress -= 1 if coup_progress >= 6; hindenburg_angry += 5; prussia_action_timer += 7
view-if: sh_banned == 0 and not prussia_gov == "Social-Catholic"

[? if president == "Hindenburg": Banning the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span> weakens our relationship with President Hindenburg, as well as the political <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> and the police. ?][? if president != "Hindenburg": Banning the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span> weakens our relationship with the political <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> and the police. ?] [? if spd_in_government = 1 and in_grand_coalition = 1 and president = "Hindenburg" : It also weakens our coalition due to the influence of Hindenburg on the <span style="color: #C0A054;">right</span> wing of our coalition. ?] In addition, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span> still operates out of public sight. 

@sunban_sh
view-if: sh_banned = 1
on-arrival: sh_banned = 0; sh_strength += 100; coup_progress += 2 if sh_coup_progress >= 6; hindenburg_angry -= 5; prussia_action_timer += 7

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span> is no longer banned.

@sban_ph
view-if: ph_banned = 0 and year == 1923
on-arrival: kpd_relation -= 10; rfb_strength -= 10; ph_banned = 1; z_relation += 3; dvp_relation += 3; ddp_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 3; prussian_police_loyalty += 0.1; dvp_left += 0.2; ddp_left += 0.3; lvp_left += 0.3; unemployed_spd -= 2; prussia_action_timer += 7

The <span style="color: [+ kpd_colour +];">Communists</span> are outraged despite having expected such a thing.

@sunban_ph
view-if: ph_banned = 1 and not prussia_gov == "Grand" and year == 1923
on-arrival: ph_banned = 0; rfb_strength += 6; prussian_police_loyalty -= 0.1; z_relation -= 3; prussia_action_timer += 7

Cool...?

@sban_rfb
view-if: communist_coalition < 3 and rfb_banned = 0 and year >= 1924
on-arrival: kpd_relation -= 15; rfb_strength -= 50; rfb_banned = 1; communist_coalition -= 1; z_relation += 5; dvp_relation += 5; ddp_relation += 5; lvp_relation += 5; prussian_police_loyalty += 0.1; dvp_left += 1; ddp_left += 0.5; lvp_left += 1; hindenburg_angry -= 8; prussia_action_timer += 7

The ban is enthusiastically carried out by the police, perhaps too enthusiastically. The <span style="color: #700000;">Communists</span> take this as one more reason why the <span style="color: #c00000;">Socialists</span> are traitors to the <span style="color: #9B0000;">left</span>. However, the <span style="color: #000000;">moderate</span> and <span style="color: #C0A054;">center-right</span> parties approve, as do the police.

@sunban_rfb
view-if: rfb_banned = 1 and not prussia_gov == "Social-Catholic" and year >= 1924
on-arrival: rfb_banned = 0; rfb_strength += 50; prussian_police_loyalty -= 0.1; hindenburg_angry += 8; prussia_action_timer += 7

The <span style="color: #700000;">Communist</span> <span style="color: #700000;">**RFB**</span> is no longer banned.

@snegotiate_concordat
view-if: (prussian_concordat_progress < 2 and z_leader != "Kaas") or (prussian_concordat_progress < 1 and z_leader = "Kaas") and prussian_concordat = 0
on-arrival: prussian_concordat_progress += 1; z_relation += 2*(1-dissent); prussia_action_timer += 7

We are making progress towards negotiating a concordat between Prussia and the Catholic church. [? if z_leader = "Kaas": Ludwig Kaas of the [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?] Party uses his connections to speed up negotiations. ?]

@ssign_concordat
view-if: (prussian_concordat_progress >= 2 and not z_leader = "Kaas") or (prussian_concordat_progress >= 1 and z_leader = "Kaas") and prussian_concordat = 0
on-arrival: prussian_concordat = 1; z_relation += 8; catholics_spd += 3*(1-dissent); catholics_dnvp -= 2 if dnvp_ideology == "Radical"; ddp_relation -= 2; ddp_cohesion -= 0.5; lvp_relation -= 2; prussia_action_timer += 10

We have signed a Concordat between the Free State of Prussia and the Roman Catholic Church, guaranteeing religious freedom for Catholics in Prussia. This sets the stage for the negotiation of a national Concordat covering all of Germany.

[? if dnvp_ideology == "Radical": The Catholic members of the <span style="color: [+ dnvp_colour +];">**DNVP**</span> in Prussia are in open conflict with their leadership over the vote, with many leaving the party. ?]












  
